    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="84.4b">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 84.4b</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84.4b" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ á<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.23"/> manna gehwylc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.29"/> to weorðunge his Drihtne do to góde þ<hi rend="italic">æt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.30"/></hi> he mæge wordes ⁊ dæde glædlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.1-2"/> æfre; þonne byð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.2-2"/> us eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> Godes milts<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.3-2"/> þe gearwur.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84.4b" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>And manna gehwylc to weorðunga his Drihtene do to gode þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he mæge wordes ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.5"/> weorces ⁊ dæde ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.star-2"/> glædlice æfre; ðonne byð us eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> God þe gearwera.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="84.4b" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="368" ed="#liebermann"/>And ha<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.3-3"/> manna gehwilc to wyrðunge his Drihtne do to gode þæs þe he mæge wordes ⁊ dæde gledlice æfre; þonne bið us eallu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> Godes miltsa þe gearwera.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="84.4b" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Et omnis homo semper ad honorem Creatoris sui faciat boni quod potest uerbo et opere hilariter usque quaque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.1"/>; et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.2"/> tunc erit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.3"/> nobis eius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.4"/> misericordia preparatior.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="84.4b" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Et semper hominum quisque in honorem sui Dei quod boni possit faciat uerbo et opere cum hylaritate; tunc erit nobis omnibus misericordia Dei paracior. . . . . . . . . .</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="84.4b" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="218" ed="#robertson"/>And<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84-4b.robnote.fn.1"/> manna gehwylc to weorðunga his Drihtene do to gode þæt<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84-4b.robnote.fn.2"/> he mæge wordes ⁊ weorces<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_84-4b.robnote.fn.3"/> ⁊ dæde<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_84-4b.robnote.fn.4"/> glædlice æfre; ðonne byð us eallum God<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_84-4b.robnote.fn.5"/> þe gearwera.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="298" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And a manna gehwylc to weorðunge his Drihtne do to gode þæt he mæge wordes and dæde glædlice æfre; þonne byð us eallum Godes milts þe gearwur.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="369" ed="#liebermann"/>Und stets thue jeder der Menschen seinem Herrgott zu Ehren immer freudig an Gutem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.de.1"/> was er kann in Wort<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_84-4b.lnote.de.2"/> (und Werk <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) und That; dann wird uns allen Gottes Gnade (Gott <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) um so bereitwilliger sein.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every person always, to the honour of his Lord God, joyfully do whatever good he can in word (and work, B) and deed; then God's mercy (God, B) will be the more ready for all of us.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="219" ed="#robertson"/>And every man, for the honour of his Lord, shall always gladly do his utmost by word and by work and by deed<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_84-4b.robnote.n.1"/> for the furtherance of what is good; then shall God be the more ready [to help us].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="299" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And to honor the Lord, each person must always gladly do all that he can to promote righteousness by word and by deed; then will God’s mercy be the more certain for us all.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">BR: added from Gesetze I p. 369, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">a: omitted B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þæt: þæs þe A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">wordes: B adds and weorces</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">dæde: B adds and Godes milts: God B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">369</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Domini <hi rend="italic">zu bessern?</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Domini to be emended?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">369</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">faceat <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">faceat Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">371</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt VIII Atr.</hi> 32 — 44; <hi rend="italic">s. o. S.</hi> 267 <hi rend="italic">f.</hi>†</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">VIII Atr. 32 — 44 follows; see above p. 267 f.†</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ w. <hi rend="italic">nicht original</hi> [<hi rend="italic">da mit</hi> ⁊ d. <hi rend="italic">synonym</hi>]; <hi rend="italic">vgl. I</hi> 19, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ w. not original [since synonymous with ⁊ d.]; cf. I 19, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.star-2" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">370</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zu streichen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to be deleted</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">371</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so KR;</hi> quaquam <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus KR; quaquam the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">371</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">371</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. eius m. erit <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. eius m. erit Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">371</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">m. e. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">m. e. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-wilce to wyrþ. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-wilce to wyrþ. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þæs ðe he <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þæs ðe he Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">370</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gledl. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gledl. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">370</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">biþ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">biþ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">370</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">miltsa ðe gearwera <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">miltsa ðe gearwera Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">368</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">gif he hwæt to gode gefremode</hi>: ‘so as to produce good’ Toller 990, 3c. 2; nicht <hi rend="italic">Gode</hi> zu schreiben</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">gif he hwæt to gode gefremode</hi>: ‘so as to produce good’ Toller 990, 3c. 2; <hi rend="italic">Gode</hi> should not be written</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_84-4b.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">214</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dieselben Worte I 19, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The same words I 19, 3</seg></note>
